Call `syncLoginItem(patch.autostart)` at :633 and `syncLoginItem(store.get('autostart'))` at :823.

findings.evidence:
:19-20 append disable-background-timer-throttling and disable-renderer-backgrounding app-wide. Their stated reason (git 215bfb2: keep the reconnect timers running in-game) doesn't hold. Reconnect and heartbeat timers are Node timers in the main process, which Chromium never throttles, and the overlay already has backgroundThrottling:false (:192). The only renderer the switches still affect is the settings window. After its first close it lives on hidden for the app's lifetime (:251-256), with:
- foreground priority and no memory purge;
- unthrottled 30 s and 60 s timers (settings.js:234 IPC poll, :366 full rebuild of the history DOM);
- every broadcast.

findings.proposed_change:
```js
// Seule la fenêtre de réglages écoute ces canaux.
function sendToSettings(channel, data) {
  if (settingsWin && !settingsWin.isDestroyed()) settingsWin.webContents.send(channel, data);
}
```
Use it in broadcastState, broadcastUpdate, recordHistory and history:clear, which removes the 4 loops. Optional: on download-progress, only broadcast update-state when the rounded percentage changed.

After the in-memory cache (store-disk-io-per-access), replace electron-store with ~25 lines. Use the same file and JSON so older versions keep reading it:
```js
const CONFIG = path.join(app.getPath('userData'), 'config.json');
let data;
try { data = { ...DEFAULTS, ...JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(CONFIG, 'utf8')) }; }
catch (e) { if (e.code !== 'ENOENT') { try { fs.renameSync(CONFIG, `${CONFIG}.corrupt-${Date.now()}`); } catch {} } data = { ...DEFAULTS }; }
function persist() {
  const tmp = `${CONFIG}.tmp`;
  try {
    fs.mkdirSync(path.dirname(CONFIG), { recursive: true });
    const fd = fs.openSync(tmp, 'w'); fs.writeSync(fd, JSON.stringify(data, null, '\t')); fs.fsyncSync(fd); fs.closeSync(fd);
    fs.renameSync(tmp, CONFIG);
  } catch (e) { console.error('[store] write failed:', e.message); }
}
```
Keep the same store.get/set/setMany facade, and remove "electron-store" from dependencies.
